-- Second paragraph: an injury made worse by an earlier illness or disability, or by late or
-- non-compliant treatment, is paid as for a person of normal health treated reasonably; a doctor's
-- conclusion is full proof of the aggravation. Encoded as an input convention: the injury table's
-- percentage supplied on the claim is the one for a person of normal health.

§ `The three layers together`

§§ `Is the claim covered`

-- Three groups of reasons, looked at in this order, the first group that has a reason giving the
-- answer (so a later group is not consulted when an earlier one already decides):
--   1. the person, the contract, the scope, the territory, the definitions, the dates;
--   2. the exclusions of Article 11;
--   3. the waiting periods of Article 10.
GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason for no payment`
`the reasons the claim is not paid` c MEANS
    IF   NOT (null (`the reasons of the person, contract and event` c))
    THEN `the reasons of the person, contract and event` c
    ELSE IF   NOT (null (`Article 11, the exclusions that apply to` c))
         THEN map (GIVEN x YIELD `excluded by` x) (`Article 11, the exclusions that apply to` c)
         ELSE IF   `Article 10, the waiting period has run` c
              THEN EMPTY
              ELSE LIST `the event fell within a waiting period (Article 10)`

GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason for no payment`
`the reasons of the person, contract and event` c MEANS
    concat (LIST
        `reason if` (NOT (`Article 1, the insured may be insured` c))
                    `the insured is not a person Article 1 admits (Articles 1, 4.1(e))`,
        `reason if` (NOT (`Article 4.1, the contract is in force on` c (c's `date of the insured event`)))
                    `the contract was not in force on the day of the event (Article 4.1)`,
        `reason if` (NOT (`the contract includes the scope of the benefit claimed` c))
                    `the contract does not include the scope this benefit belongs to (Articles 7.2, 7.3)`,
        `reason if` (NOT (`Article 7.1, the event is in the covered territory` c))
                    `the event was outside Vietnam (Article 7.1)`,
        `reason if` (NOT (`Article 7.2, the benefit answers to the cause` c))
                    `the benefit does not answer to the cause of the event (Article 7.2)`,
        `the reasons of the benefit` c)

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A `A reason for no payment`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason for no payment`
`reason if` b r MEANS
    IF b THEN LIST r ELSE EMPTY

-- What each kind of benefit needs of its own facts.
GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason for no payment`
`the reasons of the benefit` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `benefit claimed`
    WHEN `I.1 death from illness, sickness or maternity` THEN
        `reason if` (NOT (`Article 4.4, the consequence is within the contract` c (c's `date treatment began`)))
                    `the consequence arose after the contract ended (Article 4.4)`
    WHEN `III.1 hospitalisation in Western medicine` THEN `the reasons of the stay` c
    WHEN `III.2 hospitalisation in Eastern medicine` THEN `the reasons of the stay` c
    WHEN `III.3 surgery` THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the surgery`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the claim does not describe the surgery`
        WHEN JUST o  THEN concat (LIST
            `reason if` (NOT (`Article 2.19, a surgery` o))
                        `the operation is not a surgery as Article 2.19 defines it`,
            `reason if` (NOT (`Article 4.4, the consequence is within the contract` c (o's `date of surgery`)))
                        `the consequence arose after the contract ended (Article 4.4)`)
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER c's `the injury`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the claim does not describe the injury`
        WHEN JUST i  THEN `the reasons of the injury` c i

GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason for no payment`
`the reasons of the stay` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the stay`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the claim does not describe the stay`
    WHEN JUST s  THEN concat (LIST
        `reason if` (NOT (`Article 2.18, a hospitalisation` s))
                    `the stay is not a hospitalisation as Article 2.18 defines it`,
        `reason if` (NOT (`Article 4.4, the consequence is within the contract` c (s's `admission date`)))
                    `the consequence arose after the contract ended (Article 4.4)`)

-- Death after an accident is the one consequence Article 4.4 lets fall after the end of the contract.
GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
      i IS AN `An accidental injury`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason for no payment`
`the reasons of the injury` c i MEANS
    concat (LIST
        `reason if` (    c's `benefit claimed` EQUALS `II.1 death or total permanent disability from accident`
                     AND NOT (`Article 9, within 180 days of the accident` c i))
                    `the death or disability was not within 180 days of the accident (Article 9)`,
        `reason if` (NOT (`Article 2.21(b) or 2.22(b), the certification is not too early` c i))
                    `the disability was certified earlier than Article 2.21(b) or 2.22(b) allows`,
        `reason if` (    NOT (i's `consequence` EQUALS `death`)
                     AND NOT (`Article 4.4, the consequence is within the contract` c (i's `date the consequence began`)))
                    `the consequence arose after the contract ended (Article 4.4)`)

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the claim does not describe the surgery` MEANS
    REFUSE "a surgery benefit is claimed and the claim does not describe the surgery"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the claim does not describe the stay` MEANS
    REFUSE "a hospitalisation benefit is claimed and the claim does not describe the stay"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the claim does not describe the injury` MEANS
    REFUSE "an accident benefit is claimed and the claim does not describe the injury"

§§ `How much is payable`

-- The benefit of the claimed row, then the scope's cap (Article 8 II.4, III.4), then, for maternity
-- in a group contract under Article 10.2(d), the share of it.
GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Article 8, the amount payable for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `benefit claimed`
    WHEN `I.1 death from illness, sickness or maternity` THEN
        `Article 8 I.1, death from illness, sickness or maternity` c
    WHEN `III.1 hospitalisation in Western medicine` THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the stay`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the claim does not describe the stay`
        WHEN JUST s  THEN `Article 8 III.4, capped at the scope C sum insured` c
                              (`Article 10.2(d), the share of the maternity benefit` c TIMES `Article 8 III.1, hospitalisation in Western medicine` c s)
    WHEN `III.2 hospitalisation in Eastern medicine` THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the stay`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the claim does not describe the stay`
        WHEN JUST s  THEN `Article 8 III.4, capped at the scope C sum insured` c
                              (`Article 10.2(d), the share of the maternity benefit` c TIMES `Article 8 III.2, hospitalisation in Eastern medicine` c s)
    WHEN `III.3 surgery` THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the surgery`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the claim does not describe the surgery`
        WHEN JUST o  THEN `Article 8 III.4, capped at the scope C sum insured` c (`Article 8 III.3, surgery` c o)
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER c's `the injury`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the claim does not describe the injury`
        WHEN JUST i  THEN `Article 8 II.4, capped at the scope B sum insured` c (`the scope B benefit` c i)

GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
      i IS AN `An accidental injury`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the scope B benefit` c i MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `benefit claimed`
    WHEN `II.1 death or total permanent disability from accident` THEN `Article 8 II.1, death or total permanent disability from accident` c i
    WHEN `II.2 partial permanent disability from accident`       THEN `Article 8 II.2, partial permanent disability from accident` c i
    OTHERWISE                                                    `Article 8 II.3, temporary injury from accident` c i

§§ `The answer`

@export The outcome of one claim under the Tasco combined health insurance rules: not payable, with the reasons, or payable, with the amount in VND
GIVEN c IS A `A claim` @desc the policyholder, the insured, the contract, its history and state, and the insured event
GIVETH A `The outcome of a claim`
`the outcome of` c MEANS
    IF   null (`the reasons the claim is not paid` c)
    THEN `payable` (`Article 8, the amount payable for` c)
    ELSE `not payable` (`the reasons the claim is not paid` c)
